WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.940
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:05.210 --> 00:07.412
One month until the Hakone Ekiden.

3
00:07.479 --> 00:08.413
‎TOKYO-HAKONE ‎ROUND-TRIP COLLEGE EKIDEN RACE

4
00:08.480 --> 00:11.116
The Student United Team is made up

5
00:11.182 --> 00:13.918
of runners whose teams failed to qualify. Criticism is growing against

6
00:13.985 --> 00:17.255
inexperienced head coach Masato Kai.

7
00:17.322 --> 00:19.224
DUMP THE AMATEUR COACH

8
00:19.290 --> 00:20.825
This is entirely my responsibility.

9
00:20.892 --> 00:22.393
I'm sorry.

10
00:22.460 --> 00:24.462
I'm thinking of quitting as coach.

11
00:24.529 --> 00:25.563
You quit too.

12
00:26.698 --> 00:30.201
Meanwhile, at Dainichi TV, the station handling the broadcast,

13
00:30.268 --> 00:32.036
Let's do Hakone our way.

14
00:32.904 --> 00:37.675
Starting with producer Ryo Tokushige, and Broadcast Director Natsuki Miyamoto,

15
00:37.742 --> 00:38.943
the production staff,

16
00:39.010 --> 00:42.814
technical staff, and announcers press ahead with preparations…

17
00:42.881 --> 00:45.884
But some of them have other concerns.

18
00:45.950 --> 00:47.118
During that time…

19
00:47.185 --> 00:48.720
I want you as bureau chief

20
00:48.786 --> 00:50.288
-for the General Production Bureau. -Yes

21
00:51.656 --> 00:54.425
Ratings-driven Programming Bureau Chief Kuroishi

22
00:54.492 --> 00:57.962
is about to gain even more power.

23
00:58.463 --> 00:59.364
‎The results will prove it.

24
00:59.430 --> 01:02.133
Those staking everything

25
01:02.200 --> 01:04.102
on Hakone Ekiden face adversity.

26
01:23.354 --> 01:25.223
CHIEF PRODUCER RYO TOKUSHIGE

27
01:25.290 --> 01:26.291
Oh, you're up.

28
01:26.357 --> 01:29.294
That's rare. Did you drink too much?

29
01:30.094 --> 01:34.999
BROADCAST DIRECTOR NATSUKI MIYAMOTO

30
01:35.066 --> 01:37.068
32 DAYS UNTIL HAKONE EKIDEN

31
01:37.135 --> 01:38.536
-Is that the cue sheet? -Yes.

32
01:38.603 --> 01:39.437
CUE SHEET

33
01:39.504 --> 01:41.105
It's mostly set.

34
01:41.673 --> 01:44.475
I just haven't settled on the Anthology of Tales Old and New.

35
01:45.009 --> 01:46.544
Anthology of Tales Old and New, huh?

36
01:46.611 --> 01:50.148
We introduce runners and stories from past Hakone races.

37
01:51.115 --> 01:53.484
Mr. Tokushige, who stands out most in your memory?

38
01:58.289 --> 01:59.123
No answer?

39
01:59.791 --> 02:00.658
No.

40
02:01.859 --> 02:03.127
Is it Kota?

41
02:03.194 --> 02:04.062
KEITO YANO

42
02:04.128 --> 02:05.063
HAYATO AOBA

43
02:07.232 --> 02:08.099
SEIYA NAITO, SHUTO TOMIOKA

44
02:08.166 --> 02:10.368
Is Kota planning not to come back?

45
02:11.603 --> 02:12.470
DAICHI MURAI, KEISUKE NOGI

46
02:12.537 --> 02:15.406
I want all of us to run together until the end.

47
02:17.008 --> 02:17.875
Me too.

48
02:17.942 --> 02:21.079
I wonder what the other teams are doing right now.

49
02:31.122 --> 02:32.657
Next spring,

50
02:32.724 --> 02:36.995
Kuroishi becomes General Production Bureau Chief.

51
02:37.829 --> 02:40.531
It's apparently official.

52
02:40.598 --> 02:42.533
This is huge.

53
02:42.600 --> 02:43.434
YOSHIO KITAMURA

54
02:43.501 --> 02:45.837
Variety, drama, sports…

55
02:47.038 --> 02:50.808
He'll control who works on every show.

56
02:51.409 --> 02:53.244
Hey, you know too, right?

57
02:53.745 --> 02:58.883
Hakone is at the top of the shows he wants to overhaul.

58
03:00.184 --> 03:04.722
If this year's ratings come in lower than last time…

59
03:04.789 --> 03:07.358
-We'll have to brace-- -It'll be fine, Mr. Kitamura.

60
03:08.092 --> 03:09.260
What will?

61
03:09.327 --> 03:11.663
Hakone won't change.

62
03:13.231 --> 03:15.366
Don't you know?

63
03:15.433 --> 03:17.302
When he was a producer, the ratings

64
03:17.368 --> 03:20.238
for It's Showtime dipped a little.

65
03:20.305 --> 03:23.441
And he replaced all 80 staff members!

66
03:23.508 --> 03:25.777
It'll be fine!

67
03:25.843 --> 03:29.380
Bureau Chief Kuroishi… No, nobody can

68
03:29.914 --> 03:32.617
change Hakone!

69
03:42.760 --> 03:43.594
What's wrong?

70
03:43.661 --> 03:44.495
TOUGO MATSUZAWA, KOUSUKE YASUHARA

71
03:44.562 --> 03:47.365
Lately, I've been getting quizzed in the announcing department.

72
03:47.932 --> 03:48.833
Quizzed?

73
03:49.567 --> 03:50.568
Are we in grade school?

74
03:50.635 --> 03:52.437
No, it's not a game.

75
03:52.970 --> 03:54.138
I mean, it's…

76
03:54.739 --> 03:55.773
Question.

77
03:55.840 --> 03:58.276
How many curves are there in the Hakone Mountains?

78
03:58.343 --> 03:59.410
Question.

79
03:59.477 --> 04:01.846
What should you watch out for when calling Rokugo Bridge?

80
04:01.913 --> 04:03.414
Scary!

81
04:03.481 --> 04:06.150
For some reason, he's targeting me.

82
04:06.851 --> 04:08.386
That's rough.

83
04:09.153 --> 04:12.357
Hey, did you hear about the General Production Bureau?

84
04:14.125 --> 04:14.992
Yes.

85
04:16.094 --> 04:19.263
I wonder what will happen to Hakone.

86
04:19.330 --> 04:21.566
If we don't want Mr. Kuroishi messing with it,

87
04:21.632 --> 04:23.534
we need ratings.

88
04:25.002 --> 04:27.805
But beating last year's ratings these days? Come on.

89
04:50.294 --> 04:54.799
FOURTH-YEAR AT TOZAI UNIVERSITY KAZUKI AGURA

90
04:57.135 --> 04:58.836
-Thank you for your time. -Thanks.

91
04:58.903 --> 05:01.706
Coach Hirakawa, how are the runners?

92
05:01.773 --> 05:04.409
This year our depth is ridiculous.

93
05:04.942 --> 05:06.677
I'd like to make two or three teams.

94
05:06.744 --> 05:08.045
That's a lot of confidence.

95
05:08.112 --> 05:09.380
You know…

96
05:09.447 --> 05:12.617
If we had three teams, we'd finish first, second and third.

97
05:12.683 --> 05:16.854
We'd sweep the top three. That might make the race boring.

98
05:23.494 --> 05:26.030
TOZAI UNIVERSITY

99
05:26.631 --> 05:28.166
Let's pick it up at the end!

100
05:28.232 --> 05:29.200
-Okay. -Okay.

101
05:29.267 --> 05:31.803
That bad boy sure is flying.

102
05:41.646 --> 05:43.314
No luck, huh?

103
05:44.282 --> 05:45.817
Yes. Goodbye.

104
05:45.883 --> 05:49.253
ASSISTANT DIRECTOR CHIKA TOYAMA

105
05:52.890 --> 05:54.392
It's hopeless…

106
05:54.459 --> 05:56.527
Still can't find a new lunch box shop?

107
05:56.594 --> 06:00.298
It's impossible. Two hundred lunch boxes on January 2nd…

108
06:00.364 --> 06:02.967
Wait, 200 just from the cancellation? How many in total?

109
06:03.034 --> 06:06.737
966 for breakfast and 980 for lunch.

110
06:06.804 --> 06:07.705
‎Wow.

111
06:07.772 --> 06:10.141
The Hakone broadcast has that many staff?

112
06:10.208 --> 06:14.111
We deliver to more than 50 places between Tokyo and Hakone.

113
06:14.178 --> 06:17.248
So we ordered from five lunch box shops.

114
06:17.315 --> 06:20.051
I didn't expect a shop to cancel this late…

115
06:20.117 --> 06:24.288
But working on Hakone is amazing.

116
06:24.355 --> 06:26.524
My family's from Odawara.

117
06:26.591 --> 06:30.161
Every year, we all cheer from the side of the road.

118
06:30.228 --> 06:34.699
This year, I'm rooting for Tozai's new God of the Mountain, Keya!

119
06:35.733 --> 06:37.902
That smile of his is irresistible.

120
06:37.969 --> 06:39.670
-Thanks. -Thank you.

121
06:39.737 --> 06:41.606
He really is popular.

122
06:41.672 --> 06:45.243
And finally, powerhouse Tozai University is aiming for back-to-back titles.

123
06:45.309 --> 06:47.411
One runner to watch is this person.

124
06:47.979 --> 06:52.083
The Stare-Down Competitor. Captain Agura now takes him on!

125
06:52.149 --> 06:54.519
Once Agura makes his move, it's over.

126
06:54.585 --> 06:58.022
Similar to last time, I think he'll pass other runners without hesitation.

127
06:58.089 --> 07:01.359
Come on, Agura!

128
07:01.425 --> 07:03.661
The new God of the Mountain appears!

129
07:03.728 --> 07:05.463
We'll add Coach Hirakawa's comment

130
07:05.530 --> 07:07.565
from Matsuzawa here to fill the time.

131
07:08.733 --> 07:10.868
Keya's smile really is great!

132
07:10.935 --> 07:12.970
The food truck lady said she's a fan too.

133
07:13.037 --> 07:15.573
My wife and niece were screaming too.

134
07:16.073 --> 07:18.576
If we keep him on screen, won't the ratings go up?

135
07:18.643 --> 07:19.877
True.

136
07:20.411 --> 07:24.849
If we feature Keya, this year's star, viewers may stay tuned.

137
07:24.916 --> 07:27.151
Oh, the footage from Matsuzawa is in.

138
07:27.218 --> 07:28.719
-I'll send it over. -Got it.

139
07:28.786 --> 07:30.454
But next spring,

140
07:30.521 --> 07:33.624
Mr. Kuroishi might become General Production Bureau Chief.

141
07:34.725 --> 07:38.496
What will happen to Hakone? That's all anyone talks about lately.

142
07:39.096 --> 07:40.331
I'll play it now.

143
07:40.398 --> 07:43.434
This year our depth is ridiculous.

144
07:43.501 --> 07:45.269
I'd like to make two or three teams.

145
07:46.003 --> 07:48.773
Coach Hirakawa is on top of the world.

146
07:49.307 --> 07:51.108
Looks like they filmed the runners too.

147
07:51.175 --> 07:53.444
-Let me see. -Okay.

148
07:54.579 --> 07:56.213
There's the famous Keya!

149
08:00.484 --> 08:02.219
COACH HIRAKAWA

150
08:02.787 --> 08:04.422
It's Coach Hirakawa.

151
08:08.092 --> 08:09.427
Is Matsuzawa here?

152
08:09.493 --> 08:11.028
Oh, Mr. Tokushige!

153
08:11.762 --> 08:12.597
Look at this!

154
08:12.663 --> 08:14.599
We were just analyzing it.

155
08:14.665 --> 08:16.567
These are the ratings from last year's Hakone.

156
08:16.634 --> 08:19.170
Look at the fifth leg. Right here!

157
08:19.236 --> 08:20.905
It's way higher than usual.

158
08:20.972 --> 08:23.240
It's probably because Keya ran alone in the lead.

159
08:23.307 --> 08:25.610
His smile brings in serious ratings!

160
08:25.676 --> 08:27.345
That's the new God of the Mountain.

161
08:27.411 --> 08:29.547
This year, let's push Keya.

162
08:29.614 --> 08:32.717
Yes. For example, we could put a camera

163
08:32.783 --> 08:35.186
just for Keya at the Ohiradai point.

164
08:35.252 --> 08:37.488
-Matsuzawa. -Yes?

165
08:37.555 --> 08:40.257
Coach Hirakawa from Tozai University just called me.

166
08:42.259 --> 08:45.563
Is it true you made Keya run when he wasn't feeling well?

167
08:46.831 --> 08:47.832
No, that's…

168
08:47.898 --> 08:49.934
Is it true or not? Answer me.

169
08:53.104 --> 08:54.338
It's true.

170
08:55.072 --> 08:56.741
I really wanted a solo shot of him.

171
08:56.807 --> 09:01.679
But Keya said a jog would be totally fine, and so…

172
09:02.279 --> 09:03.214
Matsuzawa.

173
09:04.048 --> 09:04.882
Yes?

174
09:05.449 --> 09:07.218
Who's the star of Hakone?

175
09:09.387 --> 09:10.588
The runners.

176
09:10.655 --> 09:13.991
We never do anything that puts a burden on them.

177
09:16.093 --> 09:17.294
Right?

178
09:20.297 --> 09:21.198
I'm sorry.

179
09:24.001 --> 09:25.703
Everyone's on edge.

180
09:27.772 --> 09:29.073
It's not just Matsuzawa.

181
09:29.640 --> 09:30.474
TECHNICAL DIRECTOR TETSU KUWANA

182
09:30.541 --> 09:35.346
Everyone feels they have to do more than usual to beat last time's ratings.

183
09:39.717 --> 09:41.419
I'm sure you've all heard by now.

184
09:41.485 --> 09:44.622
Looks like the long-rumored reorganization

185
09:45.356 --> 09:49.160
will get underway next spring.

186
09:50.861 --> 09:54.398
I'm sorry the company's decision

187
09:55.599 --> 09:56.801
has worried all of you.

188
10:00.371 --> 10:03.874
But Hakone isn't that fragile.

189
10:04.942 --> 10:07.945
There have always been people telling us to change it.

190
10:08.813 --> 10:09.647
But

191
10:10.347 --> 10:12.650
we took the sash from those before us

192
10:13.684 --> 10:15.820
and kept it the same until now.

193
10:18.489 --> 10:20.257
Ratings matter, of course.

194
10:21.292 --> 10:25.362
But we have something even more important to protect. Right?

195
10:28.065 --> 10:31.635
Let's all do what we always do.

196
10:32.670 --> 10:34.405
CAMERAMAN TORU WAKAMIYA

197
10:34.472 --> 10:36.407
Well, yeah.

198
10:36.474 --> 10:40.644
Not even Bureau Chief Kuroishi would destroy Hakone.

199
10:40.711 --> 10:41.712
Right.

200
10:41.779 --> 10:43.414
It's okay, right?

201
10:43.481 --> 10:45.116
-Yes. -Yes.

202
10:48.285 --> 10:49.253
Mr. Tokushige,

203
10:49.754 --> 10:52.189
I'm really sorry.

204
10:54.692 --> 10:57.862
I'll never do anything like that again.

205
10:59.330 --> 11:00.164
‎Okay.

206
11:00.898 --> 11:01.766
I'm counting on you.

207
11:02.466 --> 11:03.667
Okay.

208
11:06.804 --> 11:10.307
A toast to Kuroishi, our General Production Bureau Chief!

209
11:10.374 --> 11:12.009
-Cheers! -Cheers!

210
11:13.577 --> 11:16.881
Hey, you're getting ahead of yourselves.

211
11:16.947 --> 11:18.949
Next spring will be here before you know it.

212
11:19.016 --> 11:20.451
You'll finally control

213
11:20.518 --> 11:23.587
-who works on every show. -Well.

214
11:23.654 --> 11:24.488
PROGRAMMING BUREAU CHIEF TAKESHI KUROISHI

215
11:24.555 --> 11:27.892
If the reforms call for it, I might do that.

216
11:29.059 --> 11:31.962
Nomura, get him to send you back to variety then.

217
11:32.029 --> 11:33.931
That's an option.

218
11:33.998 --> 11:35.099
Good for you.

219
11:35.166 --> 11:38.435
You're always saying you're sick of a younger director

220
11:38.502 --> 11:39.804
bossing you around.

221
11:40.404 --> 11:41.605
Yeah.

222
11:41.672 --> 11:42.573
Thanks.

223
11:43.207 --> 11:46.677
Is the goal for Hakone to beat last year's ratings too?

224
11:48.279 --> 11:49.346
Of course.

225
11:50.514 --> 11:52.550
Hakone doesn't get special treatment.

226
11:53.317 --> 11:56.086
But its ratings are already high.

227
11:56.153 --> 11:58.122
Beating last year will be tough…

228
11:58.189 --> 12:02.860
If they can't, I'll just break up the production team.

229
12:02.927 --> 12:04.562
Break them up?

230
12:04.628 --> 12:07.698
Maybe swap them all out for a big streaming company's sports team.

231
12:08.265 --> 12:09.200
I have ideas.

232
12:09.266 --> 12:11.168
I see.

233
12:11.235 --> 12:13.804
They've been there ten-plus years.

234
12:14.371 --> 12:18.342
Too cozy to make bold changes. That chicken.

235
12:20.911 --> 12:23.080
You really do have a lot of enemies.

236
12:23.147 --> 12:26.317
Meisei's alumni aren't too fond of you, right?

237
12:27.218 --> 12:31.455
I heard Trustee Yoneyama is objecting to you as head coach.

238
12:32.289 --> 12:34.592
I think they were surprised by the sudden change

239
12:34.658 --> 12:36.126
from Coach Moroya.

240
12:37.027 --> 12:40.097
They told me it'll be on the agenda at the general meeting after New Year's.

241
12:41.031 --> 12:42.199
Scary.

242
12:43.500 --> 12:44.468
Hey, Kai,

243
12:45.669 --> 12:47.605
why not try a fake smile now and then?

244
12:51.175 --> 12:52.176
Just kidding.

245
12:53.978 --> 12:58.115
More importantly, it's time to narrow down the ten who'll run Hakone.

246
12:58.716 --> 12:59.583
Yes.

247
13:00.417 --> 13:03.087
-But one runner concerns me. -Shuto, right?

248
13:04.121 --> 13:05.322
He's not focused.

249
13:08.759 --> 13:12.363
CHIGASAKI - LEG THREE

250
13:13.063 --> 13:16.600
‎SHUTO TOMIOKA ‎LEG THREE AND SEVEN

251
13:29.146 --> 13:30.781
Hey, Dad…

252
13:31.515 --> 13:35.252
I got picked for the Student United Team.

253
13:35.319 --> 13:36.287
ONE MONTH AGO

254
13:38.555 --> 13:39.523
So,

255
13:40.791 --> 13:43.861
I still have a chance to run Hakone…

256
13:43.928 --> 13:46.597
What's the point of running as a non-scoring entry?

257
13:47.831 --> 13:49.433
SHUTO'S FATHER KAZUTO TOMIOKA

258
13:49.500 --> 13:53.504
Don't embarrass me any more than this.

259
14:03.681 --> 14:05.816
RELAY TEST

260
14:05.883 --> 14:09.286
Hey! Show the buildings slowly!

261
14:09.353 --> 14:10.254
Yes!

262
14:10.321 --> 14:13.123
Can't you pan slowly?!

263
14:13.190 --> 14:14.091
Sorry!

264
14:14.158 --> 14:15.926
What is that garbage camera work?

265
14:15.993 --> 14:17.194
It's a little hard to see.

266
14:17.261 --> 14:18.662
Mr. Kuwa is fired up.

267
14:19.763 --> 14:23.200
Next, a shot of the chase pack from Shonan Bridge, please.

268
14:24.034 --> 14:26.870
Hey, that's the leader!

269
14:26.937 --> 14:29.773
The chase pack is near Car Three!

270
14:29.840 --> 14:30.874
Sorry!

271
14:30.941 --> 14:34.044
Car Three is yellow-green, not orange!

272
14:34.111 --> 14:35.946
It's a little hard to see.

273
14:36.013 --> 14:39.049
So the roofs of the broadcast vans are color-coded.

274
14:39.616 --> 14:42.886
From the air, runners are like specks.

275
14:42.953 --> 14:45.956
So they're color-coded to tell them apart at a glance.

276
14:46.657 --> 14:47.658
I see.

277
14:50.561 --> 14:52.162
This is Car Three.

278
14:52.229 --> 14:53.864
Raita Kuroi of Tozai University

279
14:53.931 --> 14:57.468
is racing past cheering crowds at an amazing speed!

280
14:57.534 --> 15:00.871
Oh, sorry, could you move a little more to the right?

281
15:01.805 --> 15:05.876
Coming up on the 17-kilometer point of the third leg…

282
15:05.943 --> 15:07.244
Huh? Where's the cue sheet?

283
15:07.311 --> 15:13.751
Coming into view is Hiratsuka's… something Bridge!

284
15:13.817 --> 15:14.818
Something Bridge…

285
15:14.885 --> 15:17.254
I forgot it. My notes!

286
15:18.055 --> 15:20.357
Huh?

287
15:20.424 --> 15:21.625
-Not this. -Oh, there it is!

288
15:21.692 --> 15:22.760
-Ow! -Hey!

289
15:22.826 --> 15:25.429
-Sorry! -Hey! You…

290
15:27.031 --> 15:29.900
Tanifuji, I'm not sure I can do Car Three with Matsuzawa.

291
15:29.967 --> 15:32.269
Huh? What are you talking about?

292
15:32.336 --> 15:35.939
It's Matsuzawa's debut as Car Three's director.

293
15:36.006 --> 15:38.108
But he's not taking Car Three seriously.

294
15:39.109 --> 15:40.210
Question.

295
15:41.045 --> 15:44.381
What's the bridge near the 17-kilometer point on leg three?

296
15:45.349 --> 15:46.350
Shonan Bridge!

297
15:46.417 --> 15:49.219
Correct, but in the 80th race,

298
15:49.286 --> 15:53.123
how many runners did a Kanto University athlete overtake there?

299
15:56.727 --> 15:57.628
I don't know.

300
15:58.328 --> 16:00.464
Aren't you the one not taking Car Three seriously?

301
16:03.167 --> 16:04.768
You're at Totsuka Relay Point, right?

302
16:05.769 --> 16:09.807
Question. What's a forced early start at the Hakone Ekiden?

303
16:11.775 --> 16:14.912
Once the leader passes and a set time goes by,

304
16:14.978 --> 16:18.182
the next leg's runner starts without waiting for the runner to arrive.

305
16:18.248 --> 16:21.452
Correct. But in which race did the most recent forced early start

306
16:21.518 --> 16:24.021
occur at Totsuka Relay Point

307
16:24.855 --> 16:25.989
on the return leg?

308
16:29.293 --> 16:33.931
At this rate, I won't give you Car Three or Totsuka.

309
16:35.833 --> 16:38.001
Can you two really bring Hakone to viewers?

310
16:41.305 --> 16:43.440
If that bothers you, try quizzing me.

311
16:47.711 --> 16:51.782
Hey, did you see the Hakone show on Dainichi TV yesterday?

312
16:51.849 --> 16:53.250
No, I missed it.

313
16:53.317 --> 16:54.852
You didn't miss anything.

314
16:54.918 --> 16:57.287
We weren't in it at all.

315
16:58.155 --> 17:00.891
Well, they've barely interviewed us.

316
17:01.625 --> 17:03.994
Tozai University was amazing, though.

317
17:04.061 --> 17:06.263
They followed them everywhere.

318
17:07.464 --> 17:08.899
Ugh, this sucks.

319
17:08.966 --> 17:10.300
Kota's not coming either.

320
17:10.367 --> 17:12.436
I'm so down.

321
17:18.342 --> 17:19.776
Hello.

322
17:20.344 --> 17:22.246
I'm Inagaki from Weekly Sporto.

323
17:22.312 --> 17:23.146
JOURNALIST TOMONORI INAGAKI

324
17:23.213 --> 17:25.015
You're Shuto Tomioka, right?

325
17:25.582 --> 17:27.851
Kazuto Tomioka's son?

326
17:30.087 --> 17:32.089
Your dad ran Hakone for Tozai

327
17:32.156 --> 17:34.825
and did great in the corporate leagues.

328
17:34.892 --> 17:39.229
I asked him, and he said his son wouldn't be running Hakone.

329
17:40.998 --> 17:42.366
So why are you at practice?

330
17:43.767 --> 17:45.002
Well?

331
17:47.070 --> 17:48.438
Hey.

332
17:49.273 --> 17:50.440
Answer properly, okay?

333
17:51.241 --> 17:52.743
I came all the way here to ask.

334
17:56.747 --> 17:58.415
I've got nothing to say.

335
18:01.952 --> 18:04.021
How do you get along with your dad?

336
18:04.087 --> 18:06.490
Is there a reason you didn't go to Tozai University?

337
18:08.292 --> 18:11.094
-As a result, your dad-- -Excuse me.

338
18:11.161 --> 18:13.964
Please don't do interviews without permission.

339
18:14.965 --> 18:16.867
What's the harm? Nobody else is here.

340
18:16.934 --> 18:18.402
-But… -Huh?

341
18:18.468 --> 18:21.138
We don't take questions about anything but the race.

342
18:22.339 --> 18:25.375
With all due respect,

343
18:26.009 --> 18:29.880
why ask a bunch of thrown-together weeds about the race?

344
18:29.947 --> 18:30.981
Nobody wants that.

345
18:31.048 --> 18:32.449
Please leave.

346
18:41.692 --> 18:42.626
Shuto.

347
18:45.596 --> 18:46.530
I need to talk to you.

348
18:50.934 --> 18:52.669
I'll get straight to the point.

349
18:53.904 --> 18:58.342
Does your father have something to do with your lack of focus?

350
19:05.716 --> 19:08.719
My dad has nothing to do with it.

351
19:11.355 --> 19:16.360
Tozai University has always been known as a team where results are everything.

352
19:19.129 --> 19:21.798
That's why Coach Hirakawa, an alum and the current coach,

353
19:23.267 --> 19:28.505
insists the Student United Team has no reason to run Hakone.

354
19:35.879 --> 19:37.681
This is just my guess.

355
19:38.315 --> 19:42.853
But isn't your father the same as Coach Hirakawa?

356
19:45.422 --> 19:47.858
No point running Hakone

357
19:48.525 --> 19:49.926
if it doesn't count.

358
19:53.096 --> 19:54.231
But Shuto…

359
19:57.734 --> 19:59.369
you're the one running.

360
20:07.377 --> 20:09.112
Why not run more freely?

361
20:14.951 --> 20:15.919
Excuse me.

362
20:33.570 --> 20:37.641
SEIWA INTERNATIONAL UNIVERSITY EKIDEN TEAM-SEISHIN DORMITORY

363
20:40.877 --> 20:42.112
Here?

364
20:54.057 --> 20:55.025
Kota.

365
20:55.092 --> 20:59.663
KOTA MATSUKI

366
21:02.366 --> 21:05.202
Don't show up here uninvited.

367
21:06.470 --> 21:07.537
I want to talk.

368
21:08.572 --> 21:10.173
Just give me a few minutes.

369
21:41.037 --> 21:42.005
Are you surprised?

370
21:43.173 --> 21:44.007
It's pretty shabby.

371
21:47.244 --> 21:48.245
No, it's not.

372
21:52.682 --> 21:53.650
Coach Kitano

373
21:55.252 --> 21:57.854
got this dorm with his own money.

374
21:58.855 --> 21:59.890
His own money?

375
22:01.525 --> 22:04.694
Seiwa International is a new school.

376
22:06.196 --> 22:07.798
We were a weak team.

377
22:07.864 --> 22:10.934
The Hakone Ekiden was a distant dream.

378
22:14.371 --> 22:15.772
Coach Kitano traveled

379
22:17.474 --> 22:21.645
all over the country recruiting runners.

380
22:22.145 --> 22:23.447
FIVE YEARS AGO SEIWA INTERNATIONAL UNIVERSITY

381
22:23.513 --> 22:25.015
Why not aim for Hakone with me?

382
22:26.016 --> 22:27.751
-Hakone? -Yeah.

383
22:27.818 --> 22:29.319
The Hakone Ekiden.

384
22:29.386 --> 22:30.320
KOICHI KITANO - HEAD COACH OF SEIWA INTERNATIONAL UNIVERSITY

385
22:30.387 --> 22:32.255
He wanted guys from out of town

386
22:32.889 --> 22:34.925
to have a safe place to live.

387
22:36.159 --> 22:37.160
He even took on debt

388
22:39.830 --> 22:42.766
to buy this place as a dorm.

389
22:44.301 --> 22:46.837
He even took care of our meals.

390
22:48.271 --> 22:49.172
So

391
22:50.474 --> 22:54.911
our motto was…

392
22:57.180 --> 23:01.151
"Let's take Coach to Hakone."

393
23:06.957 --> 23:09.392
I wanted to repay him for supporting us.

394
23:12.529 --> 23:14.898
That's why I ran.

395
23:17.133 --> 23:18.702
But I couldn't repay him.

396
23:21.872 --> 23:25.041
Um, can I tell you about myself?

397
23:29.446 --> 23:30.614
I'll just go ahead.

398
23:32.015 --> 23:37.254
Actually, I was a runner until my first year of college.

399
23:38.722 --> 23:39.656
But…

400
23:39.723 --> 23:43.827
MEISEI GAKUIN UNIVERSITY TRACK AND FIELD CLUB

401
23:48.198 --> 23:50.500
Hayato and the older guys were way too good.

402
23:51.501 --> 23:53.837
I knew I couldn't do it, so I gave up.

403
23:55.472 --> 23:56.573
But

404
23:57.974 --> 24:02.379
I loved track, and I didn't want to leave it.

405
24:05.048 --> 24:08.118
That's when Hayato asked me

406
24:10.086 --> 24:14.291
to join them as team manager.

407
24:17.994 --> 24:21.565
Once I tried it, it turned out to suit my personality.

408
24:23.433 --> 24:25.201
It was much more fun than I expected.

409
24:29.139 --> 24:32.475
I'm really grateful to Hayato.

410
24:37.113 --> 24:41.284
What about you, Shuto? Is running fun for you?

411
24:47.857 --> 24:48.992
To me,

412
24:51.728 --> 24:54.331
Coach Kitano means everything.

413
24:57.834 --> 25:00.236
I wouldn't be where I am without him.

414
25:05.675 --> 25:08.778
It used to be fun.

415
25:14.751 --> 25:17.387
When you grow up,

416
25:17.454 --> 25:19.522
you'll run Hakone for Tozai University like me.

417
25:19.589 --> 25:20.590
‎Okay.

418
25:20.657 --> 25:23.994
When I ran fast, he praised me.

419
25:24.594 --> 25:25.495
But…

420
25:29.466 --> 25:36.339
at some point, I started thinking he'd get mad if I didn't run fast.

421
25:40.110 --> 25:45.281
To my dad, I'm just an average…

422
25:46.483 --> 25:47.350
No,

423
25:48.885 --> 25:50.387
I'm a bottom-tier runner.

424
25:50.453 --> 25:51.388
That's not true.

425
25:57.794 --> 25:58.795
Me too.

426
26:00.330 --> 26:05.735
I've always wanted to repay Coach Moroya.

427
26:09.873 --> 26:10.774
Kota,

428
26:15.145 --> 26:22.085
I want to run Hakone trusting Coach Kai and my teammates.

429
26:25.055 --> 26:28.224
I believe that's how I can repay

430
26:28.291 --> 26:31.261
Coach Moroya too.

431
26:33.430 --> 26:34.898
And you…

432
26:34.964 --> 26:35.932
We're

433
26:37.367 --> 26:40.170
-not the same. -I know that.

434
26:42.405 --> 26:46.209
But we run for the same reason, right?

435
26:47.744 --> 26:49.345
The reason we run…?

436
26:54.250 --> 26:55.885
Honestly, I don't get it.

437
26:58.088 --> 26:59.823
"Run freely" and all that.

438
27:06.596 --> 27:09.065
I don't know if this answers it,

439
27:11.534 --> 27:13.236
but Hayato says it a lot.

440
27:17.240 --> 27:19.576
We run because we're runners, right?

441
27:29.686 --> 27:30.820
Because we're runners?

442
27:33.189 --> 27:34.357
Yes.

443
27:43.833 --> 27:47.804
Right… Adding 200 really is impossible.

444
27:47.871 --> 27:48.705
HAKONE EKIDEN

445
27:48.772 --> 27:52.575
Thank you, we appreciate it. Goodbye.

446
27:55.011 --> 27:57.580
Operation Extra Order failed too…

447
27:58.314 --> 28:00.150
Natsuki!

448
28:00.216 --> 28:01.684
27 DAYS UNTIL HAKONE EKIDEN

449
28:01.751 --> 28:03.820
Are you still fixing the cue sheet?

450
28:04.687 --> 28:07.757
You keep fixing it right up until airtime.

451
28:09.425 --> 28:12.962
Honestly, I still don't really know how to read a cue sheet.

452
28:14.264 --> 28:15.465
Done.

453
28:16.566 --> 28:20.503
Good work. Good timing. Toyama, have her show you.

454
28:20.570 --> 28:23.006
For example…

455
28:25.441 --> 28:28.044
On the first leg before Tsurumi Relay Point,

456
28:28.111 --> 28:31.281
we zoom out from the runner in the aerial shot to show Rokugo Bridge.

457
28:31.347 --> 28:34.984
Then a rear shot from Car Two shows the tough climb.

458
28:35.051 --> 28:37.320
Then Car One takes over to show the leader.

459
28:37.387 --> 28:38.388
Toyama.

460
28:38.454 --> 28:39.656
You following?

461
28:39.722 --> 28:41.057
My brain's at full capacity.

462
28:43.459 --> 28:44.294
But

463
28:45.261 --> 28:49.432
these lines are the shots you want, right, Natsuki?

464
28:50.066 --> 28:51.467
Exactly.

465
28:52.001 --> 28:55.205
What to show viewers and where.

466
28:55.271 --> 28:57.173
The broadcast director's vision

467
28:57.240 --> 28:59.309
guides 1,000 staff members.

468
29:00.210 --> 29:01.878
That's what the cue sheet is for.

469
29:02.645 --> 29:06.049
Writing cue sheets gives me a strange feeling.

470
29:07.250 --> 29:09.953
My strength alone is small,

471
29:10.019 --> 29:13.056
but linked together, it becomes big.

472
29:13.790 --> 29:17.160
It feels like a sash.

473
29:18.995 --> 29:22.265
Small strength becoming big strength…

474
29:28.137 --> 29:29.772
Broadcast system,

475
29:29.839 --> 29:31.741
-camera points… -Yeah.

476
29:31.808 --> 29:33.109
-Thank you. -Please take care of this.

477
29:33.176 --> 29:34.410
Yes.

478
29:34.477 --> 29:38.882
Tanabe is here! Zooming in with him grabbing the sash.

479
29:38.948 --> 29:41.351
His teammate is waiting right there!

480
29:41.417 --> 29:44.120
He can't let the sash break here. It carries the soul passed down

481
29:44.187 --> 29:47.123
-from his seniors. -Go!

482
29:47.190 --> 29:51.761
Yukito Tanabe is giving everything for his school and his teammates!

483
29:51.828 --> 29:54.063
Five seconds until the forced early start!

484
29:54.130 --> 29:56.499
‎Pass it!

485
29:58.001 --> 30:01.204
I'd like you to tell, in your own words,

486
30:01.271 --> 30:03.907
what happened there 17 years ago.

487
30:05.375 --> 30:07.610
I'm sorry to make this about me.

488
30:08.611 --> 30:13.750
But to me, that race and how you ran that day…

489
30:14.651 --> 30:18.888
They're special. I'll never be able to forget them.

490
30:34.103 --> 30:36.339
-Shuto… -Good morning.

491
30:38.141 --> 30:39.075
Morning.

492
30:42.478 --> 30:44.714
Shuto looks like he's having fun.

493
30:46.649 --> 30:47.483
Good morning.

494
30:47.550 --> 30:51.454
-Good morning. -Morning.

495
30:53.456 --> 30:54.691
Oh, Shuto…

496
30:56.192 --> 30:58.561
Look at him. He's all fired up.

497
30:58.628 --> 30:59.829
You're right.

498
30:59.896 --> 31:01.230
We can't lose to him.

499
31:01.764 --> 31:04.167
-Okay, let's go too! -Yeah!

500
31:07.603 --> 31:10.173
Now we just need Kota.

501
31:18.648 --> 31:20.450
Are you sure? I can go.

502
31:20.516 --> 31:23.920
It's fine. I want to do it myself.

503
31:25.088 --> 31:28.124
Hey, the Student United Team is practicing today too, right?

504
31:28.191 --> 31:30.226
Yes, I think it's at Toho University of Economics.

505
31:30.293 --> 31:31.294
Got it.

506
31:33.396 --> 31:35.932
Mr. Karashima, do you have a minute?

507
31:35.999 --> 31:37.433
We came up with some questions.

508
31:37.500 --> 31:38.701
Questions?

509
31:38.768 --> 31:41.938
You said the other day, "Try quizzing me."

510
31:43.072 --> 31:44.040
What's all this?

511
31:44.674 --> 31:50.246
Question. The record time for leg three is 59 minutes, 29 seconds.

512
31:51.080 --> 31:53.516
What is the record time for the five-kilometer point by Yugyoji?

513
31:54.083 --> 31:55.785
13 minutes, 25 seconds.

514
31:56.552 --> 31:57.520
Correct, but

515
31:58.354 --> 32:02.492
what event is held at Yugyoji every December?

516
32:02.558 --> 32:05.862
The ginkgo light-up.

517
32:06.796 --> 32:10.900
That's the level of questions you're giving me?

518
32:13.102 --> 32:16.205
Correct, but how old is the giant ginkgo

519
32:16.272 --> 32:18.474
in the center of the temple grounds?

520
32:19.075 --> 32:20.076
700 years.

521
32:20.743 --> 32:23.513
It's a designated natural monument of Fujisawa.

522
32:26.749 --> 32:28.084
Correct.

523
32:28.151 --> 32:29.652
Sorry. See you.

524
32:29.719 --> 32:30.820
But!

525
32:31.387 --> 32:35.124
That info comes from the Shonan Local History Museum.

526
32:35.691 --> 32:38.227
How old is its mascot Icchope this year?

527
32:46.769 --> 32:47.670
How should I know?

528
32:52.008 --> 32:55.244
The other day, we listened to your call

529
32:55.311 --> 32:58.748
in Car Three 15 years ago.

530
32:59.248 --> 33:03.152
This stretch is lonely. You can't even see who you're chasing.

531
33:03.219 --> 33:06.689
Strong winds between the buildings ruthlessly push the runners back.

532
33:06.756 --> 33:09.826
But now, after turning left at Shiba 5-chome,

533
33:09.892 --> 33:13.863
he can finally clearly see the back of the runner ahead.

534
33:13.930 --> 33:15.531
Those were words

535
33:15.598 --> 33:17.567
only you could say.

536
33:18.067 --> 33:23.473
I bet you walked the course many times, thinking of the runners.

537
33:25.441 --> 33:26.375
Mr. Karashima,

538
33:27.276 --> 33:31.380
we'll prepare fully as announcers

539
33:31.447 --> 33:33.249
for the main race too.

540
33:39.722 --> 33:40.723
Listen, you two.

541
33:42.291 --> 33:48.064
We announcers do all this research for one reason only.

542
33:50.666 --> 33:55.404
On race day, we show how the runners run.

543
33:56.339 --> 34:01.410
As accurately and completely as we can.

544
34:05.848 --> 34:07.316
Don't forget that.

545
34:09.585 --> 34:10.987
-Yes! -Yes!

546
34:16.726 --> 34:17.660
We did it!

547
34:19.328 --> 34:20.830
I don't know what happened,

548
34:20.897 --> 34:22.431
but good job!

549
34:22.498 --> 34:23.499
Thank you!

550
34:23.566 --> 34:25.101
Man, I was so scared…

551
34:25.168 --> 34:26.569
Everyone!

552
34:27.136 --> 34:29.138
I did it!

553
34:29.205 --> 34:30.506
What now?

554
34:30.573 --> 34:32.575
The impossible lunch box problem.

555
34:32.642 --> 34:34.944
I, Toyama, finally solved it!

556
34:35.011 --> 34:36.779
Oh, you found a lunch box shop?

557
34:36.846 --> 34:38.881
Actually, I didn't!

558
34:39.882 --> 34:42.451
I asked the four shops we had already ordered from.

559
34:42.518 --> 34:44.654
Each shop will make a little more food

560
34:44.720 --> 34:46.956
and cover a slightly larger area.

561
34:47.023 --> 34:48.991
Adding 200 is hard for one shop,

562
34:49.058 --> 34:52.695
but they all said adding 50 each is doable!

563
34:52.762 --> 34:54.630
Toyama, that's a great idea.

564
34:54.697 --> 34:56.899
-It's thanks to you, Natsuki. -Huh?

565
34:56.966 --> 34:58.501
You said it.

566
34:58.568 --> 35:00.770
One person's strength isn't much,

567
35:00.836 --> 35:03.239
but linked, it's big!

568
35:04.507 --> 35:07.343
Seriously, good job, Toyama. Nice work.

569
35:07.410 --> 35:10.947
Um, Mr. Tokushige, I'd like to ask you something.

570
35:11.814 --> 35:14.450
While researching the lunch boxes,

571
35:14.517 --> 35:16.619
I found out everyone's freezing.

572
35:16.686 --> 35:19.288
Yeah. Especially in the Odawara area.

573
35:19.355 --> 35:20.990
I wanted to do something about it.

574
35:21.057 --> 35:25.027
Remember the food truck lady? She's near the editing studio.

575
35:25.094 --> 35:26.529
Oh, the soup place.

576
35:26.596 --> 35:27.496
Yes.

577
35:27.563 --> 35:32.235
Her family is near Odawara, and they cheer by the road every year.

578
35:32.301 --> 35:34.470
So I asked, not expecting much.

579
35:34.537 --> 35:37.406
"While you're cheering, could you make some hot soup?"

580
35:37.473 --> 35:39.976
And she said yes!

581
35:40.042 --> 35:41.210
Wow, this many.

582
35:41.277 --> 35:42.812
Hot soup would really help!

583
35:42.878 --> 35:45.281
-Right? -Yeah, I'm glad!

584
35:48.684 --> 35:52.788
Broadcast van crew, please meet in the parking lot.

585
35:59.462 --> 36:00.363
What should we do?

586
36:00.429 --> 36:02.231
-What are you doing? -Oh.

587
36:03.766 --> 36:05.201
These!

588
36:05.268 --> 36:06.469
Sheets?

589
36:06.535 --> 36:10.306
He was having trouble seeing them from the helicopter.

590
36:10.373 --> 36:11.874
We replaced them after five years.

591
36:11.941 --> 36:12.775
Sorry.

592
36:12.842 --> 36:15.444
While we were at it, we covered the whole roof.

593
36:16.245 --> 36:17.847
You'll be able to see these now.

594
36:17.913 --> 36:18.814
Yes!

595
36:18.881 --> 36:20.049
I'll zoom in all I can.

596
36:21.050 --> 36:22.018
Yes, these look good.

597
36:22.685 --> 36:23.519
Sure do.

598
36:23.586 --> 36:26.822
Everyone, that's not all.

599
36:28.457 --> 36:29.925
I added hooks here

600
36:29.992 --> 36:32.862
so we can hang stopwatches for each school.

601
36:33.663 --> 36:38.601
-And the runner info is sorted by topic. -Wow!

602
36:38.668 --> 36:40.002
That's easy to follow!

603
36:40.803 --> 36:42.038
Mr. Yasuhara.

604
36:42.605 --> 36:45.775
It's my first time, so I'll probably cause a lot of trouble.

605
36:46.709 --> 36:49.478
I hope you'll work with me in Car Three!

606
36:51.447 --> 36:52.381
Sure.

607
36:54.116 --> 36:56.319
I'm jealous. I want to ride too.

608
36:56.385 --> 36:57.219
Toyama,

609
36:57.286 --> 36:59.855
-it's still too soon for you. -Why? It's okay.

610
36:59.922 --> 37:03.592
Working with this team makes me feel confident.

611
37:05.027 --> 37:09.799
Everyone is doing their best to make it a great broadcast.

612
37:12.535 --> 37:16.505
Whether that leads to ratings, I don't know.

613
37:45.868 --> 37:46.936
Kota…

614
37:50.339 --> 37:52.308
Kota…

615
37:52.375 --> 37:53.642
No way…

616
38:36.051 --> 38:36.886
Go.

617
38:58.240 --> 38:59.375
You're late.

618
39:01.010 --> 39:01.944
Sorry.

619
39:04.547 --> 39:08.884
Kota.

620
39:08.951 --> 39:12.021
Kota.

621
39:12.087 --> 39:14.990
Kota.

622
39:15.057 --> 39:19.462
Kota.

623
39:28.204 --> 39:29.071
Kota.

624
39:31.474 --> 39:32.508
Welcome back.

625
39:34.977 --> 39:36.011
Yes.

626
39:36.879 --> 39:40.983
Kota left Coach Kitano a letter saying he was quitting the team.

627
39:44.553 --> 39:48.924
I fully accept what that means.

628
39:52.728 --> 39:55.698
I'd like to take this chance to tell you all something.

629
39:58.267 --> 40:00.269
Forgive me for talking about myself.

630
40:01.270 --> 40:04.640
I want to work for something

631
40:05.774 --> 40:09.078
I can truly believe in.

632
40:11.847 --> 40:15.885
That's why I'm here now.

633
40:18.220 --> 40:20.289
There are no lies in track and field.

634
40:21.357 --> 40:23.058
The passion, determination,

635
40:23.759 --> 40:26.195
and courage to keep striving

636
40:26.896 --> 40:29.365
for faster times.

637
40:31.200 --> 40:35.237
That's where an undeniable truth lies.

638
40:37.940 --> 40:42.811
All we have to do is believe in ourselves

639
40:43.812 --> 40:44.880
and run with all we have.

640
40:47.483 --> 40:49.218
Hard work never betrays you.

641
40:52.054 --> 40:52.955
Listen.

642
40:54.089 --> 40:57.426
You're all standing at the real starting line now!

643
40:58.327 --> 40:59.628
Yes!

644
40:59.695 --> 41:02.865
It all starts here! Let's do this!

645
41:03.465 --> 41:06.168
-All right! -All right!

646
41:06.235 --> 41:09.104
-Let's show them! -That's right!

647
41:12.975 --> 41:15.444
-Go get 'em, Student United Team! -Yeah!

648
41:17.346 --> 41:19.315
It starts here for us!

649
41:41.670 --> 41:43.939
‎Regarding number 20 of Yokohama station…

650
41:44.006 --> 41:46.308
-Check beforehand with Karashima. -Okay.

651
41:47.843 --> 41:49.445
I'll leave the return leg cue sheet here.

652
41:49.511 --> 41:51.180
RETURN LEG CUE SHEET

653
41:58.787 --> 42:00.422
RETURN LEG CUE SHEET

654
42:00.489 --> 42:02.157
26 DAYS UNTIL HAKONE EKIDEN

655
42:05.227 --> 42:06.695
ANTHOLOGY OF TALES OLD AND NEW

656
42:06.762 --> 42:08.230
A SASH LEFT UNPASSED LINGERING REGRETS

657
42:11.000 --> 42:13.035
So the Anthology of Tales Old and New segment is set?

658
42:13.602 --> 42:16.138
Yes. Mr. Tokushige is out doing the interview now.

659
42:17.172 --> 42:18.173
Mr. Tokushige is?

660
42:19.441 --> 42:21.343
For this year's Anthology of Tales Old and New,

661
42:21.410 --> 42:23.679
he wanted to interview Yukito Tanabe,

662
42:23.746 --> 42:26.615
who ran Hakone 17 years ago for Kanto University.

663
42:28.550 --> 42:31.387
It was when Mr. Tokushige was director in Car Three.

664
42:32.087 --> 42:33.222
Oh, that one.

665
42:33.956 --> 42:36.825
The forced early start right before the sash relay.

666
42:37.693 --> 42:40.262
He waited, hoping to film his face

667
42:40.329 --> 42:41.664
as he passed the sash.

668
42:43.265 --> 42:47.503
He says he still can't forget Tanabe's face in that moment.

669
42:49.438 --> 42:52.875
I couldn't believe what was happening in front of me.

670
42:55.477 --> 42:57.146
-Come on, Tanabe! -You got this!

671
42:57.212 --> 43:00.049
‎-‎I could see my teammate. ‎-‎He's in the final stretch!

672
43:01.617 --> 43:03.185
He didn't make it!

673
43:03.252 --> 43:04.653
-A heartbreaking -Just a little more.

674
43:04.720 --> 43:07.056
-forced early start! -I was so close to passing it.

675
43:07.690 --> 43:09.925
"Why is this happening?"

676
43:15.564 --> 43:19.101
Kanto University's sash, carrying 75 years of tradition,

677
43:19.168 --> 43:21.570
was never passed on!

678
43:22.638 --> 43:26.241
I really wanted to pass that sash.

679
43:26.308 --> 43:27.976
You did well, Tanabe!

680
43:28.610 --> 43:30.079
I couldn't pass on the hopes

681
43:32.815 --> 43:37.419
of the seniors and my teammates.

682
43:37.486 --> 43:39.755
Even now, I… I'm sorry.

683
43:46.829 --> 43:48.097
But today,

684
43:49.631 --> 43:53.502
I feel like I can finally face

685
43:54.837 --> 43:56.538
who I was back then. A little.

686
43:58.373 --> 44:01.577
Mr. Tokushige, thank you for reaching out to me.

687
44:06.749 --> 44:07.616
Oh.

688
44:09.618 --> 44:10.853
Sorry.

689
44:10.919 --> 44:12.121
Are you okay?

690
44:12.187 --> 44:13.021
‎Yeah.

691
44:15.524 --> 44:16.525
Sorry.

692
44:18.327 --> 44:22.698
I just saw myself in you.

693
44:25.834 --> 44:31.540
My team is working so hard…

694
44:35.077 --> 44:36.111
I might not be able

695
44:40.382 --> 44:42.351
to pass the sash.

696
44:46.755 --> 44:47.723
Sorry.

697
44:57.199 --> 44:58.167
26 DAYS UNTIL HAKONE EKIDEN

698
44:58.233 --> 44:59.134
THIS DRAMA IS A WORK OF FICTION BASED ON THE HAKONE EKIDEN

699
44:59.701 --> 45:03.705
I'm leaving Dainichi TV.
